@node Abstract Syntax Tree
@section Abstract Syntax Tree

This chapter describes the internal Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) used by EIGHTBOL as its intermediate representation. All front-end languages (AGI, BASIC, Burgermistress, COBOL, FORTRAN, Lingo, Lua, Muddle, Objective-C, Pascal, SCI, SCUMM, SmallTalk, and ZIL) are parsed into this common AST structure before being processed by the code generation backends.

