@node Program Structure
@section Program Structure

The @code{:program} node represents a complete program or class definition.

@example
(:program  :class-id "Character" :data (...) :methods (...))
@end example

@table @asis
@item @code{:class-id}
The class identifier string (e.g., "Character", "PlayerClass").

@item @code{:data}
A list of data slot declarations. Each slot declaration follows the format defined in the Data Slots section below.

@item @code{:methods}
A list of method definitions. Each method follows the Method Structure format below.
@end table

Data slots are represented as property lists with the following possible keys:
@table @asis
@item @code{name}
The slot name (string or symbol).

@item @code{type}
The slot type keyword (e.g., :binary, :decimal, :object).

@item @code{size}
For binary slots: the size in bytes (1, 2, or 4).

@item @code{initial-value}
An optional initial value expression.
@end table

@node Method Structure
@section Method Structure

The @code{:method} node represents a method or procedure within a class.

@example
(:method   :method-id "Think" :statements (...))
@end example

@table @asis
@item @code{:method-id}
The method identifier string (e.g., "Think", "UpdatePosition").

@item @code{:statements}
A list of statement nodes. The first statement may optionally be an @code{:assembly-entry} node to specify the assembly entry label for this method.

Optional first statement:
@example
(:assembly-entry :label "MyRoutine")
@end example
This names the assembly entry symbol for this method body (see Programmers Reference).
@end table

@node Statement Nodes
@section Statement Nodes

This section describes all possible statement node types in the EIGHTBOL AST.

@table @asis
@item @code{(:move       :from expr :to identifier)}
Move data from source expression to target identifier.

@item @code{(:invoke     :object expr :method "Kill" [:returning identifier] [:using expr])}
Invoke a method on an object. Optional @code{:returning} specifies where to store the return value. Optional @code{:using} specifies parameters for the invocation.

@item @code{(:call-acc :target name :bank bank-or-nil)}
Call an accumulator-based subroutine or library routine. @code{:bank} is nil for local calls or a bank number/far call specification for cross-bank calls.

@item @code{(:if         :condition cond :then stmts :else stmts)}
Conditional execution. If @code{:condition} evaluates to true (non-zero), execute @code{:then} statements; otherwise execute @code{:else} statements.

@item @code{(:goto       :target identifier)}
Unconditional jump to target identifier (GOTO/GO TO). Equivalent to GOBACK when used appropriately.

@item @code{(:goback)}
Return from the current method or program (GOBACK/RETURN).

@item @code{(:exit-method)}
Exit the current method early.

@item @code{(:exit-program)}
Exit the entire program.

@item @code{(:exit)}
Generic exit (context-dependent).

@item @code{(:stop-run)}
Halt program execution with optional fault code.

@item @code{(:add        :from expr :to identifier)}
Add source expression to target identifier and store result in target.

@item @code{(:add        :from expr :to expr :giving identifier)}
Add two expressions and store result in a third identifier.

@item @code{(:subtract   :from expr :from-target identifier)}
Subtract source expression from target identifier and store result in target.

@item @code{(:subtract   :from expr :from-target expr :giving identifier)}
Subtract second expression from first and store result in third identifier.

@item @code{(:compute    :target identifier :expression expr)}
Compute expression and store result in target identifier.

@item @code{(:perform    :procedure name [:times expr] [:until cond] [:varying ...] [:body stmts])}
Perform a loop or call a procedure multiple times.
@table @asis
@item @code{:procedure}
Name of the procedure to perform.
@item @code{:times}
Exact number of iterations (optional).
@item @code{:until}
Continue until condition is true (optional).
@item @code{:varying}
Specify varying variables for counted loops (optional).
@item @code{:body}
Statements to execute in each iteration (optional).
@end table

@item @code{(:set        :target identifier :value expr)}
Set target identifier to value of expression.

@item @code{(:log-fault  :code dword-expr)}
Log a fault code for debugging purposes.

@item @code{(:debug-break :code expr)}
Trigger a debugger breakpoint with optional code.

@item @code{(:copy       :name "CopybookName")}
Residual node after failed copybook expansion.

@item @code{(:string-blt :source operand :dest operand [:length expr])}
Block transfer of string data (STRING DELIMITED BY SIZE).

@item @code{(:assembly-entry :label "Symbol")}
Must be first executable-area statement if present. Names the assembly entry symbol.
@end table

@node Expression/Operand Values
@section Expression/Operand Values

This section describes the possible values for expression operands in AST nodes.

@table @asis
@item literal number or string
Direct numeric or string literal values.

@item symbol (identifier reference)
Reference to an identifier by name.

@item (:of slot obj)
Qualified identifier (slot OF obj) for accessing object slots.

@item (:address-of id)
ADDRESS OF id - returns the memory address of identifier.

@item (:refmod :base name :start expr :length expr)
Reference modification name(start:length) for substring operations.

@item (:subscript name index)
Subscripted identifier name(index) for array access.

@item :self / :null
SELF / NULL object references.
@end table

@node FORTRAN-inspired Nodes
@section FORTRAN-inspired Node Shapes

These nodes are used by the FORTRAN frontend and feature explicit typing with no implicit numeric conversions.

@table @asis
@item @code{(:fortran-move       :from expr :to identifier :target-type type-keyword)}
Move with explicit target type specification.

@item @code{(:fortran-compute    :target identifier :expression expr :result-type type-keyword)}
Compute with explicit result type specification.

@item @code{(:fortran-declare    :name identifier :type type-keyword [:init expr])}
Variable declaration with optional initialization.

@item @code{(:fortran-do         :var identifier :from expr :to expr [:by expr] :stmts stmts)}
DO loop with explicit iteration variables.

@item @code{(:fortran-if         :condition expr :then stmts :else stmts)}
Conditional execution.

@item @code{(:fortran-logical-op :op keyword :left expr :right expr)}
Logical operation (AND, OR, etc.).

@item @code{(:fortran-arith-op   :op keyword :left expr :right expr :result-type type-keyword)}
Arithmetic operation with explicit result type.
@end table

@node Constructors
@section Constructors

This section lists the constructor functions available for building AST nodes programmatically.

@table @asis
@item @code{make-goto-node (target)}
Build a :goto AST node for GOTO/GO TO statements.

@item @code{make-program-node (class-id &key data methods identification environment)}
Build a :program AST node.

@item @code{make-method-node (method-id &key statements)}
Build a :method AST node.

@item @code{make-fortran-move (from to &optional target-type)}
Build a :fortran-move AST node with explicit typing.

@item @code{make-fortran-compute (target expression &optional result-type)}
Build a :fortran-compute AST node with explicit result typing.

@item @code{make-fortran-declare (name &key type init)}
Build a :fortran-declare AST node for variable declarations.

@item @code{make-fortran-do (var from to &key by stmts)}
Build a :fortran-do AST node for DO loops.

@item @code{make-fortran-if (condition then else)}
Build a :fortran-if AST node.

@item @code{make-fortran-type (name type &key fields)}
Build a :fortran-type AST node for structured types.
@end table

@node Accessors
@section Accessors

This section lists the accessor functions available for extracting information from AST nodes.

@table @asis
@item @code{ast-node-type (node)}
Return the node type keyword (:program, :method, :move, …).

@item @code{ast-class-id (program-node)}
Extract the class identifier from a program node.

@item @code{ast-program-id (program-node)}
Extract the program identifier from a program node.

@item @code{ast-methods (program-node)}
Extract the methods list from a program node.

@item @code{ast-data (program-node)}
Extract the data slots list from a program node.

@item @code{ast-method-name (method-node)}
Extract the method identifier from a method node.

@item @code{ast-method-statements (method-node)}
Extract the statements list from a method node.

@item @code{split-method-leading-assembly-entry (statements)}
Return (values entry-label-string-or-nil body-statements).
If the first non-NIL item in STATEMENTS is @code{(:assembly-entry :label …)},
return that label (as a string) and the remaining statements (NIL entries
removed from the head only). Otherwise return @code{(values nil cleaned)}
where @code{cleaned} is @code{(remove nil (ensure-list statements))}.

@item @code{ast-method-statements-for-validation (method-node)}
Return METHOD's statements with an optional leading @code{:assembly-entry} removed.
Used by termination validation: @code{:assembly-entry} is not executable code.
@end table

@node S-expression I/O
@section S-expression I/O

This section describes functions for reading and writing ASTs as S-expressions.

@table @asis
@item @code{write-ast (ast output-stream)}
Write AST to OUTPUT-STREAM as a readable S-expression.

@item @code{read-ast (input-stream)}
Read and return an AST S-expression from INPUT-STREAM.
@end table
